<title>USA: NY business loans fell $428 mln in Oct 9 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans fell $428 mln in Oct 9 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $428 million to $42.078 billion in the week ended October 9, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $427 million to $42.340 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $2.230 billion to $758.548 billion.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
